## Visual concept used

A **series-wired six-tier "boot-order" stack** rendered in the locked **Neural Signal Schematic** pillar style (inherited from the Cognitive track, here applied to the productivity *system* rather than the brain — no new style opened). The hero is a vertical stack of six circuit boards read **bottom-to-top, sized by leverage**: the Physical Layer is the fattest board at the floor, the AI-as-a-Worker harness is the thinnest board at the apex. A **build-current spine** climbs the left edge — lit cyan up through the highest solid tier (Knowledge System), then dim/dashed above it — carrying the rule "each layer only powers on once the one beneath reports READY" (cyan READY LEDs on lit tiers 1–4, dark LEDs on the unbuilt tiers 5–6). Every board carries the **fundamental + bolt-on × multiplier** device (thick cyan rail with a small × amplifier clipped onto it; lit on built tiers with worked examples — *inbox zero → assistant triages*, *notes you can find → RAG over your library* — and dark amber "nothing to amplify yet" on the upper tiers). The emotional reversal is the **shopping-hand-vs-build-current inversion**: a dim, stalled cursor reaches down onto the apex ("how people shop ↓") while the bright current climbs from the floor ("how you build ↑"). The **single scarce red** is the apex slop fault — an AGENT·ON chip lit over a dark base pouring out `SLOP — FASTER`. Supporting devices: a right-margin **cost-vs-return / AREA = LEVERAGE gauge** (cheap base / high return inverting to costly apex / low return), **HABITS** drawn as the earth-ground the whole stack is bonded to (a prerequisite, not a layer → Behavioral Change), the **three-pillar computer** lockup (Cognitive = hardware → Learning = software → Productivity = the OS, lit "you are here"), and two quiet grace-notes (self-improving latched memory cell `skills.md`; OS-acts ≠ Second-Brain-stores). Headline lockup: **"YOU DON'T BUY PRODUCTIVITY. YOU BUILD THE STACK."**

Deliberately **not** a pyramid and **not** an app/logo shelf, per §7 — the base is drawn fattest (the prize), the apex smallest and last to light.

